# Task git workflow

For every user task that involves code changes, before starting implementation:

1. **Create a GitHub issue** with `gh issue create` — short title + brief body describing the task. Note the issue number.
2. **Add it to the The Frame project board** (`gh project item-add 4 --owner "@me" --url <issue-url>`). Project: https://github.com/users/barzilaysapir/projects/4
3. **Branch from `preview`**, never from `main`:
   ```bash
   git fetch origin
   git checkout preview
   git pull origin preview
   git checkout -b <type>/<short-slug>
   ```
4. **Name branches** with a short type prefix: `feat/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`, `refactor/…`. Prefer including the issue number, e.g. `feat/12-routine-filters`.
5. **Link work to the issue** — mention `Fixes #N` or `Refs #N` in the PR body (and commit messages when appropriate).
6. Open the PR **into `preview`**, not `main`. Production goes `preview` → `main` only after validation. Also add the PR URL to project board `#4`.
7. **Board status**: set the issue/PR to **In Progress** when work starts; move it to **Done** when the work is finished (PR merged into `preview` and/or issue closed).

Skip this workflow only for pure questions, read-only exploration, or when the user explicitly says not to open a branch/issue.
